diff --git a/docs/REMOVAL.md b/docs/REMOVAL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/REMOVAL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Retiring citizen proposals
+
+## Deploy 1: the code
+- Removed the Proposal and dashboard models, controllers, views, routes, abilities, mailers and their English strings.
+- `ignored_columns` hides `poll_questions.proposal_id`, `map_locations.proposal_id`, `tags.proposals_count` and the proposal preferences on `users` (`recommended_proposals`, `email_digest`, `failed_email_digests_count`), so servers of this release never write them.
+- Rows other tables keep about proposals (comments, votes, follows, flags, notifications, activities) stay and are hidden by scopes, so nothing renders a record that is gone.
+- `Legislation::Proposal` is a separate feature and stays untouched.
+
+## Deploy 2: the data
+- Before the migration, `pg_dump` copied the six tables to `db/retired/tables.sql` and `psql` copied the leftover rows to `db/retired/leftover_*.csv`.
+- The migration drops the tables and those columns and deletes the leftover rows; the models of deploy 1 already ignore the columns, so servers still on deploy 1 keep working while it runs.
+
+## Deploy 3: the cleanup
+- Dropped `ignored_columns` and the scopes that hid leftover rows, since neither the columns nor the rows exist anymore.
+- The dump under `db/retired/` stays in the repository.
